# What must never reach the build context (spec 013, AC-7).
#
# The build copies the repository in, so anything listed here is something that
# would otherwise sit in an image layer on the client's box — recoverable with
# `docker history` long after it was "removed" in a later layer.

# Secrets. `.env.example` is the only one that may travel, and it carries no
# values. Written as a broad ignore and a single re-inclusion for the same
# reason the settings hook uses that shape: enumerating the real names leaves
# anything unlisted included by construction.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials that are not env files.
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# Resolved on the deps stage from the lockfile, never copied in. Copying a
# Windows-built tree into an Alpine image is also how `sharp` arrives with the
# wrong platform binaries.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Locally uploaded photographs. Gitignored, so never in the repository — but it
# is in the build context, and Next traces it into the standalone output. The
# first image carried 900K of test uploads that a volume then hid at runtime,
# which is the worst combination: shipped and invisible.
media

# Build output — regenerated inside the image. Copying a local `.next` risks
# shipping a build made with a different `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`.
.next
out

# History and tooling the runtime has no use for.
.git
.github
.husky
.claude

# Evidence and scratch. `artifacts/` holds screenshots and Playwright traces and
# is the largest directory in the repository.
artifacts
test-results
playwright-report
coverage

# Tests, specs and documentation: reviewed in the repository, not shipped.
e2e
docs
specs
packs
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__tests__
**/__golden__

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
